---
/**
 * Cookie policy page.
 * Figma: Cookie Policy / breakpoint=xl|md|base (frames 5002:22070, 53500:9561, 53500:9677)
 *
 * Copy from Figma. Headings in columns 1–6, text in 7–11 at xl; stacked below.
 */
import PageLayout from "@/layouts/PageLayout.astro";

const link = "underline underline-offset-2 text-fg-link hover:text-fg-link-hover";
---

<PageLayout page="cookie-policy">
  <section class="grid-cols-layout px-container pt-hero pb-12">
    <h1 class="col-span-full text-headline-xxl text-fg-primary xl:col-span-6 xl:col-start-7">
      Cookie Policy
    </h1>
  </section>

  <section aria-label="Cookie policy" class="px-container pb-section">
    <div class="animate-enter-stagger text-fg-primary">
      <div class="grid-cols-layout gap-y-4 border-b border-border-subtle pt-12 pb-24">
        <h2 class="col-span-full text-headline-md md:col-span-6">What are cookies</h2>
        <div class="col-span-full flex flex-col gap-5 text-body-sm md:col-span-5 md:col-start-7">
          <p>
            Like most professional websites, this site uses cookies: small files that are downloaded
            to your device to improve your experience. This page explains what information they
            collect, how we use it and why we sometimes need to store them. It also explains how you
            can stop cookies from being stored, although this may stop parts of the site from
            working properly.
          </p>
          <p>
            For more general information about cookies, see the{" "}
            <a class={link} href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HTTP_cookie">
              Wikipedia article on HTTP cookies
            </a>
            .
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="grid-cols-layout gap-y-4 border-b border-border-subtle pt-12 pb-24">
        <h2 class="col-span-full text-headline-md md:col-span-6">How we use cookies</h2>
        <div class="col-span-full flex flex-col gap-5 text-body-sm md:col-span-5 md:col-start-7">
          <p>
            We use cookies for the reasons set out below. In most cases there is no
            industry-standard way to disable cookies without also disabling the features they
            support. If you are not sure whether you need a cookie, we recommend leaving it on in
            case it supports a service you use.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="grid-cols-layout gap-y-4 border-b border-border-subtle pt-12 pb-24">
        <h2 class="col-span-full text-headline-md md:col-span-6">Disabling cookies</h2>
        <div class="col-span-full flex flex-col gap-5 text-body-sm md:col-span-5 md:col-start-7">
          <p>
            You can stop cookies from being set by changing your browser settings (see your
            browser's Help section for how to do this). Disabling cookies will affect how this site
            and many other websites work.
          </p>
          <p>
            It will usually also disable some features of this site, so we recommend that you do not
            disable cookies.
          </p>
          <p>To learn how to manage cookies, see the cookie guide for your browser.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="grid-cols-layout gap-y-4 border-b border-border-subtle pt-12 pb-24">
        <h2 class="col-span-full text-headline-md md:col-span-6">The cookies we set</h2>
        <div class="col-span-full flex flex-col gap-5 text-body-sm md:col-span-5 md:col-start-7">
          <h3>Newsletter cookies</h3>
          <p>
            This site offers a newsletter subscription. Cookies may be used to remember whether you
            are already subscribed and whether to show notifications that only apply to subscribed
            or unsubscribed visitors.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="grid-cols-layout gap-y-4 border-b border-border-subtle pt-12 pb-24">
        <h2 class="col-span-full text-headline-md md:col-span-6">Third party cookies</h2>
        <div class="col-span-full flex flex-col gap-5 text-body-sm md:col-span-5 md:col-start-7">
          <p>
            In some cases we also use cookies provided by trusted third parties. This section
            explains which third-party cookies you may encounter on this site.
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5">
            <li>
              This site uses Google Analytics, one of the most widely used and trusted analytics
              tools on the web, to help us understand how you use the site and how we can improve
              your experience. These cookies may track things such as how long you spend on the site
              and which pages you visit, so we can keep producing useful content. For more
              information about Google Analytics cookies, see the{" "}
              <a class={link} href="https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/11397207">
                official Google Analytics page
              </a>
              .
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="grid-cols-layout gap-y-4 pt-12 pb-24">
        <h2 class="col-span-full text-headline-md md:col-span-6">More information</h2>
        <div class="col-span-full flex flex-col gap-5 text-body-sm md:col-span-5 md:col-start-7">
          <p>
            We hope this has clarified things for you. As mentioned above, if you are not sure
            whether you need a cookie, it is usually safer to leave cookies enabled in case they
            support a feature you use on this site.
          </p>
          <p>
            If you have any questions, contact us at{" "}
            <a class={link} href="mailto:hello@studiocoal.com">
              hello@studiocoal.com
            </a>
            .
          </p>
          <p>
            We use cookies to personalise content, to provide social media features and to analyse
            our traffic. We also share information about your use of our site with our social media
            and analytics partners, who may combine it with other information that you have provided
            to them or that they have collected from your use of their services.
          </p>
          <p>
            The law states that we can store cookies on your device if they are strictly necessary
            for this site to work. For all other types of cookies we need your permission.
          </p>
          <p>
            Some cookies are placed by third-party services that appear on our pages. You can change
            or withdraw your consent at any time.
          </p>
          <p>
            To learn more about who we are, how you can contact us and how we process personal data,
            see our Privacy Policy.
          </p>
          <p>
            When you contact us about your consent, please include your consent ID and the date.
            Your consent applies to the following domain: studiocoal.com.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</PageLayout>
